.nh
.TH "PB-PING" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-ping - Measure authenticated connectivity to a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb ping <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Send authenticated health exchanges to one machine and print, per sample, the path used
(direct, peer_relay, regional_relay or unknown) and the round-trip time, then a loss summary.
The connection is set up before the first sample and is not part of any round-trip time.
--count sets the number of samples (1-100, default 4) and --timeout bounds each (default 10s,
at most 1m). Exit status is 1 when every sample is lost. An offline machine is an error, not a
lost sample. A reachable transport does not mean the service on the machine is ready.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--count\fP=4
	number of round trips to measure

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ping

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	timeout for each sample, the first one including connection setup


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb ping studio
  pb ping studio --count 10 --timeout 5s
  pb ping studio --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
